      "id": "thm-local-linear-transport-cauchy-problem",
      "concern": "The statement never requires sigma(eta_*)=(x_*,t_*), although the proof uses that equality in steps 1.1–2.1. As written eta_* may parametrize a different noncharacteristic point of a surface which merely passes through (x_*,t_*); data near eta_* then neither lie in a sufficiently small W about (x_*,t_*) nor determine a solution there.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    },
